# QA evidence screenshots — regenerable Playwright captures.
# NOT unreferenced: the August 2026 responsive audit cited sixteen paths inside
# this directory as its evidence. That audit was deleted on 2026-09-05 and its
# surviving facts are in docs/qa/defect-register-2026-08.md, which carries the
# method to regenerate these. They are deliberately not tracked
# (11 MB of PNGs that go stale the moment the stylesheet they document
# changes), so those citations record what was captured and at which width
# rather than linking a file you can open. Regenerate with the Method
# section of that audit.
#
# docs/qa/screenshots-mobile/ WAS tracked and was deleted on 2026-09-14: 4.3 MB
# of evidence for the sixteen defects of the 2026-08-26 mobile audit (#268),
# every one of them since fixed, showing a UI that no longer exists. The written
# findings survive in defect-register-2026-08.md, which is the part that was
# load-bearing. Both directories are now the same policy: the register records
# what was captured and at which width, and the capture itself is regenerable.
docs/qa/screenshots/
docs/qa/screenshots-mobile/

# Throwaway audit/probe scripts run from the repo root (module resolution
# needs them here). Never committed.
__*.mjs
__*.py

# Third-party skills installed by `npx skills add` (2026-09-03:
# Leonxlnx/taste-skill, 13 skills). This is a package manager's install
# directory — treat it like node_modules and reinstall rather than commit.
#
# Two concrete reasons, not a preference:
#   1. `npx skills add` symlinks .claude/skills/<name> -> .agents/skills/<name>
#      with an ABSOLUTE target (/d/00_Main_Workspace/...). Committed, those
#      links resolve to nothing on any other machine and in CI.
#   2. Git on Windows handles symlinks poorly — without core.symlinks=true they
#      land as plain text files containing a path, which is worse than absent
#      because it looks like content.
#
# How they are used, and where the codebase overrides them, is documented in
# docs/reference/doc-authority-map.md. Reinstall with:
#   npx skills add Leonxlnx/taste-skill
.agents/
.claude/skills/brandkit
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend
.claude/skills/design-taste-frontend-v1
.claude/skills/full-output-enforcement
.claude/skills/gpt-taste
.claude/skills/high-end-visual-design
.claude/skills/image-to-code
.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-mobile
.claude/skills/imagegen-frontend-web
.claude/skills/industrial-brutalist-ui
.claude/skills/minimalist-ui
.claude/skills/redesign-existing-projects
.claude/skills/stitch-design-taste
# pbakaus/impeccable, added 2026-09-04 by the same package manager.
.claude/skills/impeccable
# ...and the lockfile that package manager writes alongside them.
skills-lock.json
tests/flakeprobe-a0e1/artifacts/

# local screenshot harness (agent scratch)
shoot-tmp.mjs
mi-tmp.mjs

# scripts/firebase-deferral-trial.mjs — temporary copies of the two gated
# contexts with docs/design/firebase-deferral-gated.patch applied, plus the
# wrapper config that aliases them in. All three are deleted when it finishes;
# ignored so a crashed run cannot leave a second auth implementation in the
# tree looking like reviewed code.
src/**/*.trial.jsx
vite.config.trial.mjs
.firebase-deferral-trial.patch

# Scratch directories the gated-patch appliers use. Both copy the founder-gated
# files somewhere writable, apply a diff there, and delete the directory in a
# `finally` — these lines exist so a crashed run cannot leave a half-patched
# copy of firestore.rules sitting in `git status` looking like reviewed code.
.tmp-rules-patch-*/
.tmp-gated-patch-*/
.tmp-gated-diff-*/

# Impeccable live-mode session state and journal. Durable for the tool,
# not project source, and it holds absolute machine paths.
.impeccable/

# Screenshots and image archives — LOCAL ONLY.
#
# Measured 2026-09-15: screenshots/ was 8.7 MB across 27 tracked files, and
# eleven of the fifteen largest tracked files in the whole repository were the
# June portfolio archive. Nothing under src/, scripts/, api/, tests/ or public/
# reads any of them — the only references are three prose mentions in docs/,
# which describe what the shots showed rather than embedding them.
#
# They are kept on disk and out of git: a design archive is worth having and is
# not worth carrying in every clone, every CI checkout and every deploy.
screenshots/
*.psd
*.sketch
*.fig
